 friendship  then he says this fire ain't hot enough  it's just lukewarm and that he's going  to instead go temper himself in the  legendary fires of the flame of ruin  which for you lore experts out there  should sound pretty familiar and this is  why you can then summon him again for  the fight against the fire giant who was  guarding the flame of ruin before you  killed him after which you now have  access to said flame of ruin and  apparently using the flame transports  you to the timeless city held in midair  called the crumbling pharaoh missoula  because whether you let melana light the  flame using her body as kindling or you  do it yourself in the path of the  frenzied flame you end up in fair  missoula either way meaning doing this  equals portal to here anyway apparently  alexander also tried to use the frenzied  flame to temper himself because you run  into him up there but this unfortunately  marks the last time your paths will  cross because his path ends here you see  the whole time you've been meeting up  with alexander at different points in  the game he always says that he wants to  fight stronger champions in order to  become stronger himself right but the  strongest champion he's ever seen is  standing right in front of him it's you  so he formally asks you if you would do  him the honor of facing him in mortal  combat which ends of course with your  victory after the battle lying on the  ground moments from death he says he  knew he never really stood a chance  against you but that he was glad he got  to go out the warrior's way and with one  last hearty chuckle he shatters  completely leaving behind the shard of  alexander that i spoke about earlier and  a bloody clump of his insides and while  this marks the tragic end of iron fist  alexander's story what about its  beginning is there any way to find out  more about where he came from and why he  was so obsessed with becoming a strong  warrior absolutely there is if you  travel to the eastern region of lyonia  at the bottom of a cliff that is much  too tall for any normal being to descend  without carefully stepping from one  outcrop to the next you will find a  hidden village that is not accessible  any other way this quaint little village  is called jarburg and it is the home of  the living jars that alexander came from  and vowed to never return to but unlike  the other soul jars you come across in  the game that either try to punch you or  blow you up or otherwise end your  existence the jars of jarburg are all  100 friendly docile and town right  adorable citizens of the lands between  you'll find them lying about idly  chatting with one another and even  dancing around flowers they're so cute  one of these jars in particular is a  youth named jar baron who you can  actually walk up to and speak with the  little jar affectionately refers to you  as cuz short for cousin and asks if  you're there to be the new potentate of  jarburg potentate means leader by the  way but will then deny you your potency  on account of your not having smooth  hands i should have been using lotion  before too long jar baron will ask you  if you've met uncle alexander and will  then explain to you that alexander used  to live there in jarburg but then left  to become a champion and insisted that  the path of the champion must be taken  alone and in classic alexander fashion  vowed to never again return home his  bravery and heroic ambition inspired the  little jar baron who admits to you  secretly that he too is a warrior jar  and one day will also leave the village  to become strong just like his uncle  alexander please don't tell anyone cuz  but  i'm actually a warrior jar as well but  why should these jars living in  essentially jar heaven leave are they  just getting bored well possibly but jar  baron also gives us some insight into  this question he eventually asks you if  you've heard of the poachers who hunt  down living jars and smash them up for  their pieces this 